      ":question/problem": "![](images/07/07aaf788552b002f804b98558a79a2951ac091897539093bbffc0063a2289897.png)\n\nThe curve ${C}_{1}$ has endpoints $A(1,-1)$ and $B(-1,1).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=x\\,i+(1-y)\\,j$ through ${C}_{1}$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector ${n}_{1},$ as shown above.\n\n*Hint: You're given that $F$ is source-free, and the segment $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ can be parametrized as*\n\n$$\nr=(1-2t)\\,i+(-1+2t)\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$"
